{
  "wasim_version": "0.1.0",
  "source": {
    "generator": null,
    "notes": "Two correlated GBM assets and a spread option priced by Monte Carlo, with the exchange option (Margrabe) as a control variate. Correlated standard normals are built with the 2x2 Cholesky construction of Glasserman Sec 2.3 (Z2 = rho*Z1 + sqrt(1-rho^2)*Zi), keeping rho a live input that also drives the Margrabe closed form. run_stat2 is used twice: corr(Z1,Z2) as a live self-check that the correlation is reproduced, and beta(exchange,spread) as the control-variate coefficient. The exchange-option Margrabe price (live via erf) is both the validation reference and the control's known mean. See CORRELATED_ASSETS_EXAMPLE.md."
  },
