      "description": "Correlated standard normal via the 2x2 Cholesky construction (Glasserman Sec 2.3): Z2 = rho*Z1 + sqrt(1-rho^2)*Zi has unit variance and Corr(Z1,Z2)=rho, with rho a LIVE input. WASiM also has a native `correlations` field (Gaussian copula) as an alternative; the explicit Cholesky here keeps rho editable and mirrors the text.",
